{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Milcah as well</b> — Because she was the daughter of Haran, his brother, this was tidings to Abraham that his elder brother had been remembered with many children, unlike the daughter of his deceased brother. And from the language of the verse it appears that he did not know about any of them until this day, and if their having children had occurred in their youth, it is impossible that he would not have heard of them until now, for the distance between Aram Naharaim and the land of Canaan is not great. Now Abraham, when he went forth from Haran, was seventy-five years old, and Nahor too was old and his wife was no longer young, but HaShem performed a miracle for them in that they were remembered with children in old age. This is the reason for \"Milcah as well,\" and in the words of our Sages (Yalkut Shimoni, remez 526) it means that she was remembered as her sister was remembered:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The Yalkut Shimoni reference תשסו resolves to remez 526 by gematria."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:28.571759875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}